# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify the budget cyclically {#specify-the-budget-cyclically}"
msgstr "Tentukan budget secara siklik {#specify-the-budget-cyclically}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you have a circuit with some repeatable pattern, such as a Trotter circuit, you might want to specify a budget for that repeated subset of slices and have that budget used for all of the following repetitions of those slices.\n"
msgstr "Kalau kamu punya circuit dengan pola yang berulang, seperti circuit Trotter, kamu mungkin ingin menentukan budget untuk subset slice yang berulang itu dan memakai budget tersebut untuk semua pengulangan slice berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More concretely, the example circuit we are using has six slices that are repeated three times, for a total of 18 slices. We will arbitrarily assign zero budget to the single-qubit and `RYY` layers, and `.003` budget to each of the `RXX` layers. We will observe how specifying the budget as a length-6 sequence causes the budget to be applied to all 18 slices cyclically.\n"
msgstr "Lebih konkretnya, contoh circuit yang kita pakai punya enam slice yang diulang tiga kali, totalnya 18 slice. Kita akan menetapkan budget nol secara sembarang untuk layer satu-qubit dan `RYY`, dan budget `.003` untuk tiap layer `RXX`. Kita akan melihat bagaimana menentukan budget sebagai urutan sepanjang 6 membuat budget diterapkan ke semua 18 slice secara siklik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Again, note that the slices are backpropagated in reverse order (that is, starting at the end). Therefore, the first entry in our cyclic budget actually gets used for the last slice, the second entry for the slice before that, and so on.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Sekali lagi, perhatikan bahwa slice di-backpropagate dalam urutan terbalik (yaitu, mulai dari akhir). Jadi, entri pertama di budget siklik kita sebenarnya dipakai untuk slice terakhir, entri kedua untuk slice sebelumnya, dan seterusnya.\n"
"</div>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As seen in the **top left** and **bottom left** images, no truncation was performed over the first four slices since they were allocated no error budget. Slices five and six had some of their terms truncated as budget became available.\n"
msgstr "Seperti terlihat di gambar **kiri atas** dan **kiri bawah**, tidak ada pemangkasan pada empat slice pertama karena slice tersebut tidak dialokasikan error budget. Slice lima dan enam punya beberapa suku yang dipangkas begitu budget tersedia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As seen in the **top left** image, a relatively large amount of error was incurred after backpropagating slice seven, even though that slice was allocated no budget. This is because only about `.002` of the `.006` total budget allocated to slices five and six was used, so the remaining was forwarded to slice seven and mostly expended, as seen in the **top right** image.\n"
msgstr "Seperti terlihat di gambar **kiri atas**, error yang muncul cukup besar setelah backpropagation slice tujuh, padahal slice itu tidak dialokasikan budget. Ini karena hanya sekitar `.002` dari total budget `.006` yang dialokasikan ke slice lima dan enam yang terpakai, sehingga sisanya diteruskan ke slice tujuh dan hampir habis terpakai, seperti terlihat di gambar **kanan atas**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **top left** and **top right** images show that the small amount of leftover budget is used up between slices 8-10, and new budget becomes available in slice 11, as expected. The **top left**, **top right**, and **bottom left** images all demonstrate the cyclical behavior of the `max_error_per_slice` argument when its length is less than the number of slices. This cyclical behavior would have continued through all the slices, but the `max_qwc_groups` stopping criteria was reached after backpropagating 13 slices, as seen in the **bottom right** image.\n"
msgstr "Gambar **kiri atas** dan **kanan atas** menunjukkan bahwa sedikit sisa budget habis terpakai di antara slice 8-10, dan budget baru tersedia di slice 11, seperti yang diharapkan. Gambar **kiri atas**, **kanan atas**, dan **kiri bawah** semuanya memperlihatkan perilaku siklik dari argumen `max_error_per_slice` saat panjangnya kurang dari jumlah slice. Perilaku siklik ini akan berlanjut sampai semua slice, tapi kriteria berhenti `max_qwc_groups` tercapai setelah backpropagation 13 slice, seperti terlihat di gambar **kanan bawah**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Also interesting is that the number of Pauli groups actually drops after the second round of budget becomes available at slice 11. This is because there were groups with small coefficients that could not be truncated until there was more budget after backpropagating slice 11, so they accumulated in the observable for several iterations. This case also highlights that `max_qwc_groups` must be _exceeded_ for the algorithm to terminate.\n"
msgstr "Yang juga menarik, jumlah grup Pauli justru turun setelah putaran kedua budget tersedia di slice 11. Ini karena ada grup berkoefisien kecil yang tidak bisa dipangkas sampai ada lebih banyak budget setelah backpropagation slice 11, sehingga grup-grup itu menumpuk di observable selama beberapa iterasi. Kasus ini juga menyoroti bahwa `max_qwc_groups` harus _dilampaui_ agar algoritma berhenti.\n"

