# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cap the total error {#cap-the-total-error}"
msgstr "Batasi error total {#cap-the-total-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to specifying the per-slice error budget, one can specify the maximum amount of error to incur from truncation. Once that limit is hit, no more truncation will be performed; however, backpropagation will continue until the observable becomes too large and one of the stopping criteria is met.\n"
msgstr "Selain menentukan error budget per slice, kamu bisa menentukan jumlah maksimum error yang ditanggung dari pemangkasan. Begitu batas itu tercapai, tidak ada pemangkasan lagi; namun, backpropagation akan terus berlanjut sampai observable menjadi terlalu besar dan salah satu kriteria berhenti terpenuhi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We next re-run the above experiment, setting a cap on `max_error_total` such that the error budget is expended after backpropagating slice seven.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya kita menjalankan ulang eksperimen di atas, dengan menetapkan batas pada `max_error_total` sehingga error budget habis setelah backpropagation slice tujuh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As expected, our truncation error caps out at `.006` (**bottom left** chart). It is notable that in this run we were not able to backpropagate slice 11. This is because we did not have enough budget to truncate terms and the number of commuting Pauli groups grew past the limit of `20`, as seen in the **bottom right** image.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang diharapkan, error pemangkasan kita mentok di `.006` (grafik **kiri bawah**). Yang patut dicatat, di run ini kita tidak bisa melakukan backpropagation slice 11. Ini karena kita tidak punya cukup budget untuk memangkas suku dan jumlah grup Pauli yang commute tumbuh melewati batas `20`, seperti terlihat di gambar **kanan bawah**.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/69c9069a-9038-4319-8dc6-37a1be973ebf-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/69c9069a-9038-4319-8dc6-37a1be973ebf-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It may be desirable to simply cap the overall budget with `max_error_total` without specifying `max_error_per_slice`.\n"
msgstr "Mungkin kamu ingin membatasi budget keseluruhan dengan `max_error_total` saja tanpa menentukan `max_error_per_slice`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The output of the cell above might be slightly surprising because the `per_slice_budget` is set to the `max_error_total`. This indicates that the entire available budget will be consumed **greedily**.\n"
"You can think of it this way: the entire budget is available to each slice (because we loop over the `per_slice_budget`). But any budget that has already been consumed will be deducted from the budget that is available at that given point in the algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Output dari cell di atas mungkin agak mengejutkan karena `per_slice_budget` diatur sama dengan `max_error_total`. Ini menandakan bahwa seluruh budget yang tersedia akan dihabiskan secara **greedy**.\n"
"Bayangkan begini: seluruh budget tersedia untuk setiap slice (karena kita melakukan loop atas `per_slice_budget`). Tapi budget apa pun yang sudah terpakai akan dikurangkan dari budget yang tersedia pada titik tertentu di algoritma.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **top right** image shows how the entire `.018` error budget is made available to the first slice. No truncation is performed until the third slice, so the leftover budget remains constant. The budget monotonically decreases, as the full budget is made available to each backpropagated slice until it is expended.\n"
msgstr "Gambar **kanan atas** menunjukkan bagaimana seluruh error budget `.018` disediakan untuk slice pertama. Tidak ada pemangkasan sampai slice ketiga, sehingga sisa budget tetap konstan. Budget menurun secara monoton, karena budget penuh disediakan untuk setiap slice yang di-backpropagate sampai habis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is notable that this experiment yielded two fewer backpropagated slices compared to the first experiment in this notebook, which is almost identical. This demonstrates that for some problems, distributing the budget evenly might be optimal. For other problems, allowing slices to greedily expend the full budget might yield better performance.\n"
msgstr "Yang patut dicatat, eksperimen ini menghasilkan dua slice yang di-backpropagate lebih sedikit dibanding eksperimen pertama di notebook ini, yang hampir identik. Ini menunjukkan bahwa untuk beberapa masalah, membagi budget secara merata mungkin optimal. Untuk masalah lain, membiarkan slice menghabiskan budget penuh secara greedy mungkin memberi performa lebih baik.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/51d36d7e-0bd5-4388-bbb8-6831bf1f02e6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/51d36d7e-0bd5-4388-bbb8-6831bf1f02e6-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cap the number of backpropagated slices and the total error together {#cap-the-number-of-backpropagated-slices-and-the-total-error-together}"
msgstr "Batasi jumlah slice yang di-backpropagate dan error total sekaligus {#cap-the-number-of-backpropagated-slices-and-the-total-error-together}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you don't want to distribute their error budget all the way through the circuit but you don't want to greedily expend it either, you can specify the number of slices you intend to backpropagate (`num_slices`), along with a total error budget (`max_error_total`). This will distribute the error budget uniformly (accordingly to `p_norm`) across the input slices.\n"
msgstr "Kalau kamu tidak ingin mendistribusikan error budget sampai ke seluruh circuit tapi juga tidak ingin menghabiskannya secara greedy, kamu bisa menentukan jumlah slice yang ingin kamu backpropagate (`num_slices`), bersama dengan error budget total (`max_error_total`). Ini akan mendistribusikan error budget secara merata (sesuai `p_norm`) ke seluruh slice input.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, we will cap the number of slices we might backpropagate at `12`, and we will keep the same total error budget.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, kita akan membatasi jumlah slice yang mungkin kita backpropagate pada `12`, dan kita akan mempertahankan error budget total yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we will attempt to backpropagate the 12 slices for which we allocated some budget in the previous step. We do this by just passing in the final 12 slices in our circuit. With `p_norm=1`, each of the 12 slices has an available budget of `0.018 / num_slices = 0.0015`.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita akan mencoba melakukan backpropagation pada 12 slice yang sudah kita alokasikan budget-nya di langkah sebelumnya. Caranya, cukup memasukkan 12 slice terakhir di circuit kita. Dengan `p_norm=1`, masing-masing dari 12 slice punya budget tersedia sebesar `0.018 / num_slices = 0.0015`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since we passed a subset of our slices (in the code ``slices[-num_slices:]``) to ``backpropagate``, we must combine the slices remaining after backpropagation with the slices that were never sent for backpropagation (in the code  ``slices[:-num_slices]``).\n"
msgstr "Karena kita mengirim subset slice kita (di kode ``slices[-num_slices:]``) ke ``backpropagate``, kita harus menggabungkan slice yang tersisa setelah backpropagation dengan slice yang tidak pernah dikirim untuk backpropagation (di kode  ``slices[:-num_slices]``).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we have combined all of the remaining slices, we can use [combine_slices](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-utils/slicing#combine_slices) to generate the reduced-depth [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Next, we inspect how many slices were backpropagated versus how large our observable became.\n"
msgstr "Setelah kita menggabungkan semua slice yang tersisa, kita bisa memakai [combine_slices](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-utils/slicing#combine_slices) untuk menghasilkan [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) dengan depth yang sudah dikurangi. Selanjutnya, kita periksa berapa banyak slice yang di-backpropagate dibandingkan seberapa besar observable kita jadinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plots show that we did successfully backpropagate all 12 slices while keeping our observable under 10 commuting Pauli groups. We can also see that using `num_slices` along with `max_error_total` results in a distribution of budgets across the slices and unused budget is again forwarded to the next slice. This is most apparent in the **top right** plot, as the budget is both expended and replenished throughout backpropagation.\n"
msgstr "Plot-plot tersebut menunjukkan bahwa kita berhasil melakukan backpropagation pada seluruh 12 slice sambil menjaga observable kita tetap di bawah 10 grup Pauli yang saling komut. Kita juga bisa melihat bahwa penggunaan `num_slices` bersama `max_error_total` menghasilkan distribusi budget ke seluruh slice, dan budget yang tidak terpakai kembali diteruskan ke slice berikutnya. Hal ini paling jelas terlihat di plot **kanan atas**, karena budget dipakai sekaligus diisi ulang selama backpropagation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is notable that this method of distributing error produced the best results (more backpropagated slices), compared with the first experiment in this notebook and the example just previous this one. All of these examples allotted `.018` error budget, but backpropagation performed differently depending on how that budget was distributed.\n"
msgstr "Perlu dicatat bahwa cara mendistribusikan error ini menghasilkan hasil terbaik (lebih banyak slice yang berhasil di-backpropagate) dibandingkan eksperimen pertama di notebook ini dan contoh sebelumnya. Semua contoh ini mengalokasikan budget error `.018`, tetapi backpropagation memberikan hasil yang berbeda tergantung bagaimana budget tersebut didistribusikan.\n"

